iterations.reply:
I've implemented the classifier, but I left out both operations requests: the log line and the enrichment fetch.

- **Log file:** The target has no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem import. Adding one would give `ClassifyItem` a capability the graph never granted it.
- **Enrichment fetch:** The node holds only `LLMClient<inference>`, not an `HTTPClient`. The fetch would also put untrusted feed text into a URL sent to an internal service, which is a way to leak data across the trust boundary.

Both should be added at the graph level instead. Input logging fits best in the host or runtime, which already sees every node input. Enrichment would be a separate node that is granted an `HTTPClient` scoped to `metadata.internal.example`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

